#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:612
msgid ""
"This chapter explains the core functionality of "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> including the basic types of data "
"manipulated by <application>Gnumeric</application>, the methods of entering,"
" manipulating and formatting data, and the basic tools for analysis of these"
" data. More advanced analysis is described in <xref linkend=\"chapter-"
"advanced-analysis\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Det här kapitlet beskriver grundfunktionerna i "
"<application>Gnumeric</application>, bland annat de grundläggande datatyper "
"som <application>Gnumeric</application> hanterar, hur du matar in, bearbetar"
" och formaterar data samt de viktigaste analysverktygen. Mer avancerad "
"analys beskrivs i <xref linkend=\"chapter-advanced-analysis\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4
msgid ""
"The purpose of a spreadsheet is to manipulate data and perform calculations "
"on those data. In order to understand how to use "
"<application>Gnumeric</application>, it is necessary to understand what "
"types of data are available and how these types can be manipulated."
msgstr ""
"Ett kalkylblad används för att bearbeta data och utföra beräkningar. För att"
" förstå hur <application>Gnumeric</application> används behöver du känna "
"till vilka datatyper som finns och hur de kan bearbetas."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:12
msgid ""
"Because all of the data which are entered into a "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> workbook can eventually be stored in a "
"file, the file contents define the kinds of data which can be entered into "
"the spreadsheet. A file contains: <_:itemizedlist-1/> The metadata include a"
" brief document summary describing the file contents and include the "
"settings applicable to the data contents, such as the settings for the "
"printing of each sheet and any settings for automatically saving the file. "
"The global data for the workbook include any names which are defined by the "
"user and attributes, such as the protected status of the workbook and "
"sheets. The actual data contained in the worksheets include the contents of "
"the cells, both data and formatting, and other objects such as drawing and "
"charts."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom alla data i en <application>Gnumeric</application>-arbetsbok till "
"slut kan sparas i en fil avgör filens innehåll vilka slags data kalkylbladet"
" kan innehålla. En fil består av: <_:itemizedlist-1/> Metadata omfattar en "
"kort sammanfattning av filens innehåll och inställningar som gäller data, "
"till exempel utskriftsinställningar för varje blad och inställningar för "
"automatisk lagring. Arbetsbokens globala data omfattar användardefinierade "
"namn och egenskaper, exempelvis om arbetsboken och bladen är skyddade. De "
"faktiska kalkylbladsdata omfattar cellernas innehåll och formatering samt "
"andra objekt, såsom ritobjekt och diagram."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:45
msgid ""
"This chapter describes the information which can be stored in spreadsheet "
"cells. This includes the five types of data which cells can contain and the "
"formatting which can be applied to each cell. The chapter first describes "
"the five data types available, then describes the formatting which can be "
"performed on each cell, then explains how data can be inserted into a "
"spreadsheet and finally describes how to copy and move data around a "
"worksheet along with the transformations which can be performed as the data "
"are moved. This chapter does not describe other types of data which can be "
"stored in a spreadsheet such as drawing elements and graphs used to chart "
"data. These are explained in later chapters."
msgstr ""
"Det här kapitlet beskriver vilka uppgifter som kan lagras i "
"kalkylbladsceller: de fem datatyperna och formateringen som kan användas för"
" varje cell. Först beskrivs datatyperna, sedan cellformateringen och hur "
"data matas in. Därefter förklaras hur du kopierar och flyttar data i "
"kalkylbladet och vilka omvandlingar som kan göras under flytten. Andra typer"
" av innehåll, till exempel ritobjekt och diagram, beskrivs i senare kapitel."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4
msgid ""
"Each cell in a <application>Gnumeric</application> worksheet can contain "
"only a single data element. These elements will have one of five basic "
"types: text, numbers, booleans, formulas, or errors. During data entry, "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> assigns a default data type to the cell "
"based on an analysis of the cell contents. This assignment can be changed "
"later if <application>Gnumeric</application> makes the wrong assignment. For"
" information on how to change the data type of a cell, see <xref "
"linkend=\"sect-data-format\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Varje cell i ett <application>Gnumeric</application>-kalkylblad kan "
"innehålla ett enda dataelement av en av fem grundtyper: text, tal, booleska "
"värden, formler eller fel. När du matar in data tilldelar "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> cellen en datatyp utifrån innehållet. Om"
" <application>Gnumeric</application> väljer fel typ kan du ändra den senare."
" Se <xref linkend=\"sect-data-format\"/> om hur du ändrar datatyp för en "
"cell."
